# WHAT `helm package` LEAVES OUT OF THE PUBLISHED TARBALL (yaadgaar 169).
#
# `ci/` is CI input, not chart content (ADR-0806): `ci/values.yaml`,
# `ci/estate-values.yaml` and `ci/api-versions.txt` are read from the git
# checkout by the helm-lint hook, the trivy gate and every other consumer, never
# from the tarball. helm never renders `ci/`, so this changes no render.
#
# `charts/` is NOT ignored: the vendored subcharts are the package's content,
# and `test_the_package_carries_every_declared_subchart` proves they ship.
#
# `LICENSES/` and `NOTICE` are NOT ignored either: they are the licence texts
# of those vendored subcharts, so they must ship beside them (yaadgaar 377).
# `test_the_package_carries_the_licences_and_the_notice` proves they do.
ci/
.git/
*.tgz.prov
